    skos:definition "(2) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person threatens to use force or violence against a group (the targeted group); and (b) the targeted group is distinguished by race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, intersex status, disability, nationality, national or ethnic origin or political opinion; and (c) a reasonable member of the targeted group would fear that the threat will be carried out. Note: For intention, see section 5.2. Penalty: Imprisonment for 5 years."@en ;
