concept:criminal-code-amendment-hate-crimes-act-2025-sch-1-sec-80-3-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "80(6) 2BA  Threatening force or violence against groups"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-80-3-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) Subsection (7) applies if, in a prosecution for an offence (the prosecuted offence) against subsection (1), the trier of fact: (a) is not satisfied that the defendant is guilty of the offence; but (b) is satisfied beyond reasonable doubt that the defendant is guilty of an offence (the alternative offence) against subsection (2).  Amendments  Schedule 1  No. 1, 2025 Criminal Code Amendment (Hate Crimes) Act 2025" ;
    skos:definition "(6) Subsection (7) applies if, in a prosecution for an offence (the prosecuted offence) against subsection (1), the trier of fact: (a) is not satisfied that the defendant is guilty of the offence; but (b) is satisfied beyond reasonable doubt that the defendant is guilty of an offence (the alternative offence) against subsection (2).  Amendments  Schedule 1  No. 1, 2025 Criminal Code Amendment (Hate Crimes) Act 2025"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "752988219d8d54379de6dac13ed6aca7fd38fc8a6002241c38924172df116388" ;
    values:partOf concept:criminal-code-amendment-hate-crimes-act-2025-sch-1-sec-80-3 ;
    cof:pageNumber "11"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Prosecution must consider alternative offence beyond reasonable doubt if trier of fact is not satisfied with defendant's guilt." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <criminal-code-amendment-hate-crimes-act-2025.pdf> ;
    dc:source "criminal-code-amendment-hate-crimes-act-2025.pdf, p.11" ;
    cml:asserts concept:criminal-code-amendment-hate-crimes-act-2025-sch-1-sec-80-3-ss-6-norm .
