doc:sch-1-sec-80-3-ss-6 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "80(6) 2BA  Threatening force or violence against groups" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(6) Subsection (7) applies if, in a prosecution for an offence (the prosecuted offence) against subsection (1), the trier of fact: (a) is not satisfied that the defendant is guilty of the offence; but (b) is satisfied beyond reasonable doubt that the defendant is guilty of an offence (the alternative offence) against subsection (2).  Amendments  Schedule 1  No. 1, 2025 Criminal Code Amendment (Hate Crimes) Act 2025" ;
    cof:pageNumber "11"^^xsd:integer .

concept:criminal-code-amendment-hate-crimes-act-2025-sch-1-sec-80-3-ss-7 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "80(7) 2BA  Threatening force or violence against groups"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-80-3-ss-7 ;
    values:originalText "(7) The trier of fact may find the defendant not guilty of the prosecuted offence but guilty of the alternative offence, so long as the defendant has been accorded procedural fairness in relation to that finding of guilt. Definitions" ;
    skos:definition "(7) The trier of fact may find the defendant not guilty of the prosecuted offence but guilty of the alternative offence, so long as the defendant has been accorded procedural fairness in relation to that finding of guilt. Definitions"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "937d5d9835542f78fbb35632b15f03dae19b1bce6420dccb2221b64614386d8e" ;
    values:partOf concept:criminal-code-amendment-hate-crimes-act-2025-sch-1-sec-80-3 ;
    cof:pageNumber "11"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Triier of fact must accord procedural fairness in relation to finding of guilt." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
