doc:sch-1-sec-80-4-ss-7 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "80(7) 2BB  Threatening force or violence against members of groups or" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(7) Subsection (8) applies if, in a prosecution for an offence (the prosecuted offence) against subsection (1), the trier of fact: (a) is not satisfied that the defendant is guilty of the offence; but (b) is satisfied beyond reasonable doubt that the defendant is guilty of an offence (the alternative offence) against subsection (2)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "13"^^xsd:integer .

concept:criminal-code-amendment-hate-crimes-act-2025-sch-1-sec-80-4-ss-8 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "80(8) 2BB  Threatening force or violence against members of groups or"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-80-4-ss-8 ;
    values:originalText "(8) The trier of fact may find the defendant not guilty of the prosecuted offence but guilty of the alternative offence, so long as the defendant has been accorded procedural fairness in relation to that finding of guilt.  Amendments  Schedule 1  No. 1, 2025 Criminal Code Amendment (Hate Crimes) Act 2025 Definitions" ;
    skos:definition "(8) The trier of fact may find the defendant not guilty of the prosecuted offence but guilty of the alternative offence, so long as the defendant has been accorded procedural fairness in relation to that finding of guilt.  Amendments  Schedule 1  No. 1, 2025 Criminal Code Amendment (Hate Crimes) Act 2025 Definitions"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f5007e20bc6d7731c5d940226316bd2cb002910eec5278848ffa87d4f7eab9a6" ;
    values:partOf concept:criminal-code-amendment-hate-crimes-act-2025-sch-1-sec-80-4 ;
    cof:pageNumber "13"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Procedural fairness in relation to finding of guilt" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
