concept:criminal-code-amendment-hate-crimes-act-2025-sch-1-sec-80-7-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "80(5) 2BE  Advocating force or violence through causing damage to"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-80-7-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) Subsection (6) applies if, in a prosecution for an offence (the prosecuted offence) against subsection (1), the trier of fact: (a) is not satisfied that the defendant is guilty of the offence; but (b) is satisfied beyond reasonable doubt that the defendant is guilty of an offence (the alternative offence) against subsection (2)." ;
    skos:definition "(5) Subsection (6) applies if, in a prosecution for an offence (the prosecuted offence) against subsection (1), the trier of fact: (a) is not satisfied that the defendant is guilty of the offence; but (b) is satisfied beyond reasonable doubt that the defendant is guilty of an offence (the alternative offence) against subsection (2)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "806282e440068fde7a66f3f512c5d378b40172025c41e2b157836127d9ca8853" ;
    values:partOf concept:criminal-code-amendment-hate-crimes-act-2025-sch-1-sec-80-7 ;
    cof:pageNumber "20"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Trier of fact must be satisfied beyond reasonable doubt that defendant is guilty of alternative offence." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
